# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BACKUP OUTPUT -- never commit this.
#
# The default output directory sits next to the script, so it lands inside this
# repository. It contains PRIVATE OSF projects and unpublished data, possibly
# human-subjects material covered by an IRB protocol. Publishing it would be
# hard to undo: git history retains deleted files, and anything pushed to a
# public remote should be assumed permanently disclosed.
#
# If you point OSF_OUTPUT_DIR somewhere with a different name, add that name
# here too -- this file cannot guess it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
osf_backup_results/
osf_backup_results_public/

# Older / alternate output directory names, kept so an existing backup made
# before the default was renamed cannot be committed by accident.
osf_backup/
osf_backup_collab/

# Backup artifacts, wherever they land.
#
# These catch the case where OSF_OUTPUT_DIR points at a differently-named
# folder inside the repo: the directory rule above would not match it, but
# these filenames are unmistakably backup output. Nothing in this project
# legitimately produces a .zip, so excluding all of them is the safe default —
# a downloaded archive is the single worst thing to publish by accident.
**/*.zip
**/backup_manifest.csv
**/problems_found.csv
**/problems_found_offline.csv
**/verification_report.csv
**/offline_verification_report.csv
**/scope_report.txt
**/checksums.csv
**/metadata.json
**/contributors.json
**/logs.json
**/wikis.json
**/registration.json
**/preregistration.md
**/DOI.txt
**/*.part
**/*.partial.*

# Credentials
.Renviron
.env

# R / RStudio
.Rproj.user/
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata

# macOS
.DS_Store
._*

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*~
*.swp

# Local scratch tooling and notes, not part of the project
rcheck.py
scratch_readme.md
